WEBVTT


00:02:30.051 --> 00:02:34.545
- I can't believe this.
- Why not?


00:02:34.606 --> 00:02:37.682
Because I love you, Fabio, like a son.


00:02:37.683 --> 00:02:41.245
And I love you, Don Luis, like a father.


00:02:43.186 --> 00:02:45.575
I'm going to miss you.


00:02:46.392 --> 00:02:49.068
And I'm going to miss you.


00:02:50.171 --> 00:02:51.271
Okay,


00:02:51.272 --> 00:02:53.240
enough of this sentimental bullshit.


00:02:53.241 --> 00:02:57.951
One last drink?
Next, we'll be crying like two old women!


00:02:57.952 --> 00:02:59.760
Come on.


00:03:00.342 --> 00:03:02.661
To the future.


00:03:03.911 --> 00:03:06.454
<i>Good health and life!</i>


00:03:12.877 --> 00:03:15.260
So, business is all clear?


00:03:18.682 --> 00:03:21.019
It's all here.


00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:26.976
- No other copies?
- You have to ask? -Hey!


00:03:27.078 --> 00:03:29.785
Come on.


00:03:35.380 --> 00:03:37.815
I'm going to miss you.


00:03:37.883 --> 00:03:40.204
<i>Bye, Marco.</i>


00:03:49.559 --> 00:03:51.457
Kill this motherfucker.


00:03:58.914 --> 00:04:02.347
<i>I cannot believe this.</i>


00:04:03.837 --> 00:04:05.730
Not okay, boss?


00:04:05.731 --> 00:04:08.948
The bastard thinks I'm an idiot,
playing it all mellow and shit.


00:04:08.949 --> 00:04:11.526
If he would have yelled and screamed
and threatened to kill my whole family...


00:04:11.527 --> 00:04:13.227
it would've been better.


00:04:13.698 --> 00:04:16.831
<i>We have about an hour to get
outta here at the most! Let's go!</i>


00:04:52.122 --> 00:04:54.347
We've got ten minutes.


00:04:54.828 --> 00:04:58.976
- Cataleya, go pack.
- I'm packed Mamma.


00:05:10.103 --> 00:05:12.166
Cataleya.


00:05:13.258 --> 00:05:16.917
<i>Listen to me.
In case anything happens...</i>


00:05:16.918 --> 00:05:20.513
this is your passport.


00:05:20.514 --> 00:05:24.612
If you find yourself alone,
you go to this address on this card.


00:05:24.613 --> 00:05:27.598
Show it to the man at the gate.


00:05:28.499 --> 00:05:32.620
- I don't understand, Papa.
- You don't have to understand.


00:05:32.621 --> 00:05:36.588
You just have to listen
and remember.


00:05:37.962 --> 00:05:43.371
Take the bus and go here.


00:05:47.938 --> 00:05:52.395
And this... this will keep you safe.


00:05:53.389 --> 00:05:57.138
The cataleya orchid.
My mother, your grandmother...


00:05:57.139 --> 00:06:03.875
used to grow them. Every morning I'd wake
up to the sight of them. The smell of them.


00:06:04.585 --> 00:06:08.292
That's why I named you 'Cataleya'.


00:06:08.680 --> 00:06:11.463
Never forget where you came from.


00:06:27.838 --> 00:06:30.372
Hi. We want to see Don Fabio.


00:06:30.373 --> 00:06:32.547
He's not home.


00:06:34.372 --> 00:06:38.023
<i>- I'm ready.
- It's time! Come! Come!</i>


00:06:38.024 --> 00:06:41.249
- Let's go!
- Come on.


00:06:48.432 --> 00:06:50.406
Back, back, back.


00:06:56.223 --> 00:06:58.544
They say he is not home yet.


00:06:58.545 --> 00:07:00.232
Wait a minute.


00:07:00.985 --> 00:07:04.545
It's too late.
Get ready.


00:07:10.865 --> 00:07:14.471
I love you very much.


00:07:16.115 --> 00:07:18.724
I love you too, Papa.


00:07:22.820 --> 00:07:25.159
Do it now.


00:07:25.584 --> 00:07:28.037
Change of plans.


00:09:08.131 --> 00:09:11.919
Do you remember me, Cataleya?


00:09:12.893 --> 00:09:15.619
I was at your confirmation.


00:09:15.620 --> 00:09:19.734
My name is Marco
and I was a very good friend of your father.


00:09:20.371 --> 00:09:25.225
You know who Don Luis is, right?


00:09:25.229 --> 00:09:28.557
He was like a father to your father.


00:09:28.572 --> 00:09:31.551
That makes you family too.


00:09:32.876 --> 00:09:40.797
But... when... someone...
is good to you...


00:09:40.898 --> 00:09:44.890
and you're not good to them back,
then bad things happen.


00:09:46.732 --> 00:09:48.596
You do very well in school,


00:09:48.597 --> 00:09:52.297
so I know this is not too complicated
for you to understand. Am I Right?


00:09:53.431 --> 00:09:55.105
Excellent.


00:09:55.106 --> 00:10:02.129
Now, your father had something that belonged
to Don Luis. It's a small thing.


00:10:02.130 --> 00:10:04.244
Not bigger than this.


00:10:04.369 --> 00:10:06.720
Do you know where it is?


00:10:08.451 --> 00:10:09.651
Well,


00:10:09.952 --> 00:10:16.141
if you give it to me, Don Luis will be
very happy and very grateful.


00:10:16.771 --> 00:10:23.285
So... why don't you just give me that
little thing, which belongs to him.


00:10:24.266 --> 00:10:26.041
Would you do that?


00:10:26.042 --> 00:10:28.493
You're a smart girl.


00:10:28.494 --> 00:10:34.936
And in this life smart girls
always get what they want.


00:10:36.190 --> 00:10:40.184
Just tell me, sweetheart...


00:10:40.215 --> 00:10:42.343
What do you want?


00:10:44.811 --> 00:10:47.629
To kill Don Luis!


00:10:54.388 --> 00:10:57.018
Grab that little bitch.


00:11:04.195 --> 00:11:06.373
We need her alive.


00:11:20.722 --> 00:11:23.686
Find her! Find the little bitch.


00:13:20.353 --> 00:13:22.805
Do not stop.


00:13:26.010 --> 00:13:28.041
Got you.


00:14:27.158 --> 00:14:29.107
Excuse me.


00:14:40.193 --> 00:14:44.325
And you said you...
you have something for us, sweetie?


00:14:46.927 --> 00:14:49.281
Well, may I see it?


00:15:33.369 --> 00:15:35.880
Okay, everybody,
take a five-minute coffee break.


00:15:37.237 --> 00:15:39.872
Jim, we're gonna have to record this.


00:15:43.276 --> 00:15:46.862
- Where did you get this?
- My Papa.


00:15:47.003 --> 00:15:48.969
where is your Papa?


00:15:49.011 --> 00:15:51.093
Dead.


00:15:51.924 --> 00:15:53.695
Do you know what this is?


00:15:53.696 --> 00:15:55.563
Yes.


00:15:55.564 --> 00:15:58.294
My passport.


00:16:04.397 --> 00:16:07.077
We're about to arrive in Miami.


00:16:08.237 --> 00:16:10.143
I'll buckle you up.


00:16:25.620 --> 00:16:27.735
Welcome to America.


00:16:36.262 --> 00:16:38.648
Go ahead, I'll wait right here.


00:17:09.017 --> 00:17:12.771
Hello, young lady, where are we wanting
to go today?


00:17:15.578 --> 00:17:19.070
Chicago? That's not just down the street,
you know?


00:17:19.910 --> 00:17:21.934
How much?


00:18:16.181 --> 00:18:19.866
Hey, kid, what are you doing here?


00:18:42.993 --> 00:18:45.820
Emilio.


00:18:51.897 --> 00:18:54.115
There's a girl looking for you.


00:18:55.820 --> 00:18:59.371
It does not matter.


00:19:03.013 --> 00:19:05.472
Her name is Cataleya.


00:19:31.375 --> 00:19:35.654
- Cataleya...
- Tio?


00:20:07.577 --> 00:20:09.914
I thought you were dead.


00:20:15.062 --> 00:20:17.155
You're safe.


00:20:19.695 --> 00:20:23.035
It's okay.
You're safe now.


00:20:23.560 --> 00:20:25.473
You're safe.


00:21:06.388 --> 00:21:13.134
You have your mother's beautiful eyes.


00:21:14.416 --> 00:21:16.783
Don't be afraid.


00:21:17.339 --> 00:21:20.018
This is your home.


00:21:26.369 --> 00:21:29.174
How long has it been since you sleep?


00:21:29.175 --> 00:21:32.348
I don't know. A long time ago.


00:21:32.349 --> 00:21:35.437
Well, good.
A young body needs to sleep.


00:21:35.438 --> 00:21:39.133
When I was your age,
I would sleep half the day.


00:21:39.895 --> 00:21:41.587
I don't know if it helps
with your growing pattern,


00:21:41.588 --> 00:21:44.588
but I was always ready
for what came after.


00:21:48.003 --> 00:21:52.196
Whose room did I sleep in?


00:21:53.657 --> 00:21:55.873
My son.


00:21:55.874 --> 00:21:58.328
Your cousin.


00:21:58.588 --> 00:22:01.384
Where is he?


00:22:03.214 --> 00:22:05.924
He's dead.


00:22:07.470 --> 00:22:09.505
Killed?


00:22:11.982 --> 00:22:13.927
Yes.


00:22:14.528 --> 00:22:16.369
By whom?


00:22:16.991 --> 00:22:20.230
No one who is still alive.


00:22:23.835 --> 00:22:25.704
You are very talented.


00:22:25.705 --> 00:22:30.965
- Is this what you want to be, an artist?
- I used to want to be like Xena.


00:22:30.966 --> 00:22:33.705
A Warrior Princess.


00:22:34.039 --> 00:22:36.566
Not any more?


00:22:38.797 --> 00:22:41.223
No?


00:22:43.369 --> 00:22:45.769
I want to be a killer.


00:22:49.362 --> 00:22:51.417
Can you help?


00:22:53.389 --> 00:22:55.765
Sure.


00:23:12.253 --> 00:23:16.544
Normally we don't accept students
in the middle of the academic year.


00:23:16.547 --> 00:23:23.748
But under these circumstances,
losing her parents in a tragic car accident.


00:23:24.650 --> 00:23:27.847
Here you are. These are...
the school supplies you'll need.


00:23:27.848 --> 00:23:29.147
Sorry...


00:23:29.148 --> 00:23:31.189
She's a little traumatized.


00:23:31.190 --> 00:23:32.599
Of course.


00:23:32.600 --> 00:23:35.006
See you Monday, Cataleya.


00:23:35.635 --> 00:23:37.892
Such a pretty name.


00:23:40.302 --> 00:23:42.618
Thanks.


00:23:46.010 --> 00:23:48.745
After we get all this stuff,
we go over to Maxwell Street...


00:23:48.746 --> 00:23:51.746
to get hot dogs
from those Polish people here.


00:23:51.747 --> 00:23:53.147
You like hot dog?


00:23:57.489 --> 00:23:59.325
What is it now?


00:23:59.326 --> 00:24:02.132
That school has nothing to teach me.


00:24:02.133 --> 00:24:05.011
I told you what I want.


00:24:05.812 --> 00:24:08.886
You don't want to help me? Fine.


00:24:08.887 --> 00:24:11.496
I'll do it myself.


00:24:13.525 --> 00:24:16.101
Look.


00:24:28.688 --> 00:24:30.332
See that?
Is that what you want?


00:24:30.333 --> 00:24:34.733
You want me to teach you how to be
a killer? Sure, no problema, I'll teach you.


00:24:34.933 --> 00:24:38.178
But you'll be dead in five years.


00:24:41.007 --> 00:24:45.313
If you want to be a killer and survive,
you got to be a smart one.


00:24:46.035 --> 00:24:48.817
You have to know things besides
how to pull a trigger.


00:24:48.818 --> 00:24:51.048
You have to know how the world works,
how people think...


00:24:51.049 --> 00:24:53.233
You gotta learn how to stand,
how to be psychological.


00:24:53.234 --> 00:24:56.833
And I cannot teach you that
unless you learn the basics out of school.


00:24:56.834 --> 00:24:59.579
You got that? Hmm?


00:24:59.726 --> 00:25:02.929
Come on. What's it going to be?
Cataleya? You choose.


00:25:02.930 --> 00:25:05.026
Come on.


00:25:05.238 --> 00:25:08.066
Now. Choose.


00:25:08.067 --> 00:25:11.900
What you want? Choose.


00:25:20.369 --> 00:25:22.927
Better.


00:25:47.233 --> 00:25:49.980
Hey, buddy.
I got the good stuff.


00:25:49.981 --> 00:25:52.500
- So, might I suggest...
- Yeah?


00:25:52.501 --> 00:25:54.184
Let's buy some things.
You know,


00:25:54.185 --> 00:25:56.902
spice it up a bit,
like we talked about.


00:25:56.903 --> 00:25:57.845
Some of those stockings...


00:25:57.846 --> 00:25:59.740
- that come up to the thigh.
- Right, nice.


00:25:59.741 --> 00:26:01.833
It's been fourteen years,
you know what I mean?


00:26:01.834 --> 00:26:03.766
No matter how much you like steak...


00:26:03.767 --> 00:26:06.493
sometimes a lamb chop
isn't a bad thing, right?


00:26:06.494 --> 00:26:08.244
Exactly.


00:26:14.620 --> 00:26:17.519
Son of a bitch!


00:26:26.466 --> 00:26:31.495
- Put your hands on the car!
- Hands on the vehicle, right now!


00:26:31.553 --> 00:26:33.976
Oooh, back...


00:26:36.110 --> 00:26:39.029
- Stupid, crazy bitch.
- I'm really sorry.


00:26:39.030 --> 00:26:41.929
This is not...
it's not even my car.


00:26:41.930 --> 00:26:45.070
- You think this is funny?
- No, sir!


00:26:46.350 --> 00:26:49.809
I'm gonna give you something to laugh about.


00:26:50.139 --> 00:26:53.745
I'm sorry, officer.
I'm sorry, I don't drink...


00:27:15.512 --> 00:27:17.730
There's nothing here.


00:27:18.079 --> 00:27:23.684
No license, no registration, No ID...


00:27:23.685 --> 00:27:27.120
except for a library card.


00:27:27.121 --> 00:27:30.651
Miss Valerie Philips.


00:27:30.652 --> 00:27:33.493
In addition to all that,
you are being charged with,


00:27:33.494 --> 00:27:37.593
D.U.I. driving on the wrong side
of the road and...


00:27:37.594 --> 00:27:39.680
the destruction of police property.


00:27:41.413 --> 00:27:43.760
Miss Philips!


00:27:43.761 --> 00:27:46.022
Do I have your full attention?


00:27:48.621 --> 00:27:51.619
Yeah...
That's it?


00:27:52.170 --> 00:27:55.503
Unless there's anything else
you can think of?


00:27:56.585 --> 00:28:00.328
- I have to throw up.
- Oh, no, no, no. Get her out of here.


00:28:01.577 --> 00:28:03.822
And a cup of coffee too.
We can book her tomorrow.


00:28:03.823 --> 00:28:07.473
Let her sleep it off,
for Christ's sake...


00:28:16.555 --> 00:28:18.925
Alright, big step. Down you come.


00:28:19.773 --> 00:28:22.997
Alright, stretch those legs. Come on, move!


00:28:25.493 --> 00:28:27.272
McGee just checked downstairs.


00:28:27.273 --> 00:28:29.581
She's from Rome, okay?
And she says to the other...


00:28:29.582 --> 00:28:31.476
Excuse me. U.S. Marshall Warren.


00:28:31.477 --> 00:28:33.928
We're here with Gennaro Rizzo
on an overnight.


00:28:33.979 --> 00:28:35.929
Wait, wait, wait...
hold on a second.


00:28:36.041 --> 00:28:38.906
You know, it says here that
you're not expected until tomorrow.


00:28:38.907 --> 00:28:41.197
Yeah, well, never expect
the expected, sergeant.


00:28:41.198 --> 00:28:42.697
Is that coffee there?
Is that fresh?


00:28:42.698 --> 00:28:44.660
- Yes, it is.
- Do you mind?


00:28:44.661 --> 00:28:45.811
My treat.


00:28:46.161 --> 00:28:47.532
- Appreciate it.
- You know, uh...


00:28:47.533 --> 00:28:50.272
Officer Doyle is gonna show you
where the cell blocks are.


00:28:50.273 --> 00:28:51.804
Oh, come on.


00:28:53.453 --> 00:28:54.997
Home, sweet home.


00:28:59.298 --> 00:29:02.158
After you, sir.


00:29:10.275 --> 00:29:12.697
I'm going to miss you, Rizzo.


00:29:12.698 --> 00:29:16.559
I gonna leave that just there,
just in case you get hungry in the night.


00:29:18.000 --> 00:29:19.865
Sleep well.


00:29:19.866 --> 00:29:23.837
This'll be a caffeine kinda night, Joe.
Keep your eyes open.


00:32:02.069 --> 00:32:04.380
Two...


00:32:04.381 --> 00:32:06.761
Three...


00:32:10.359 --> 00:32:11.582
Not again.


00:32:11.633 --> 00:32:14.499
Hey, Doyle, go check
on the ventilation system, will you?


00:32:14.850 --> 00:32:17.100
As in today, please?


00:33:16.313 --> 00:33:18.976
- Yeah?
- Yeah, I gotta pee...?


00:34:25.495 --> 00:34:28.196
- Unbutton your shirt... Now.
- What?


00:34:32.102 --> 00:34:34.796
Who are you?


00:34:41.383 --> 00:34:43.309
Go! Come on!


00:34:43.318 --> 00:34:46.004
We have a security threat.


00:34:46.676 --> 00:34:49.269
Come!


00:34:49.846 --> 00:34:52.776
Get inside.
Somebody open the fucking door!


00:35:00.420 --> 00:35:03.320
Look at me, Joe, look at me.
Give me the gun.


00:35:03.321 --> 00:35:06.197
Just give it to me, OK. It's good.


00:35:07.144 --> 00:35:10.585
- Hold on, hold on.
- I didn't do it.


00:35:10.586 --> 00:35:12.538
I didn't do it!.


00:35:13.813 --> 00:35:17.745
- Get him out of here.
- I didn't do it!


00:35:17.746 --> 00:35:20.503
Call it in. Call it in!


00:36:14.963 --> 00:36:16.919
Damn.


00:36:33.751 --> 00:36:36.304
Check on the other side.


00:36:39.304 --> 00:36:41.553
It's clear here.


00:37:04.822 --> 00:37:07.150
I'm outta here.


00:37:25.426 --> 00:37:27.326
Agent Ross.


00:37:27.327 --> 00:37:30.117
- Where is he?
- He's in the morgue.


00:37:30.118 --> 00:37:32.088
Let's go.


00:37:38.603 --> 00:37:40.731
This is just how he came in.


00:37:43.413 --> 00:37:45.837
It's the same handwriting.


00:37:49.123 --> 00:37:51.337
Same drawing, right?


00:37:51.439 --> 00:37:53.497
That's him.


00:37:54.244 --> 00:37:56.975
I want to see the location, please.


00:37:57.557 --> 00:37:59.121
Thank you.


00:38:01.121 --> 00:38:03.791
- Oh, I shouldn't drink.
- No, you shouldn't.


00:38:03.873 --> 00:38:05.873
Oh, God, I'm so sorry.


00:38:05.874 --> 00:38:09.972
Yeah, you can tell that to the Judge
in ten days' time, at your hearing.


00:38:12.911 --> 00:38:14.116
What's going on down there?


00:38:14.117 --> 00:38:17.216
Nothing. You can sign this form,
and then you can go.


00:38:17.217 --> 00:38:18.354
- Really?
- Yeah, really,


00:38:18.355 --> 00:38:20.654
but I'm quite sure
the judge will send you back here.


00:38:20.655 --> 00:38:24.035
- I'd probably deserve it.
- Oh, you're just lucky no one got hurt.


00:38:30.810 --> 00:38:32.241
Okay, now, back up.


00:38:40.606 --> 00:38:41.810
You're gonna have to lock it down.


00:38:42.111 --> 00:38:44.310
Hey, it was after the fact,
I didn't think anybody would...


00:38:44.311 --> 00:38:47.917
You gotta do it, okay?
Nobody in, nobody out, please.


00:38:49.907 --> 00:38:53.879
You heard that man. Lock it down.
Nobody in or nobody out.


00:39:27.767 --> 00:39:33.178
I wanna see paper, on everybody in
and outta this station in the last 24 hours.


00:39:37.615 --> 00:39:39.594
And I want the tapes.


00:39:39.595 --> 00:39:42.340
From all the security cameras.


00:39:42.341 --> 00:39:44.213
All of them.


00:40:28.783 --> 00:40:31.600
<i>- It's all okay?
- We're good.</i>


00:40:31.601 --> 00:40:34.138
- When you're back?
- The day after tomorrow.


00:40:34.439 --> 00:40:36.798
Look, I have something for you.


00:40:37.624 --> 00:40:38.740
Give me a day.


00:40:38.940 --> 00:40:39.840
Okay.


00:40:40.141 --> 00:40:41.792
We can't wait to see you back.


00:40:42.984 --> 00:40:45.678
- Give mama a kiss for me.
- I will.


00:40:51.962 --> 00:40:55.178
Twenty-two murders in the last four years
all with the same MO.


00:40:55.479 --> 00:40:57.843
I think I'm right,
he is sending a message...


00:40:57.844 --> 00:40:59.843
but I'm beginning to believe
it's not meant for us.


00:40:59.844 --> 00:41:02.084
Well, we're the only ones
with that information.


00:41:02.085 --> 00:41:04.185
Well, we're not getting anywhere
with it, are we?


00:41:04.285 --> 00:41:06.718
Put it out to the press.
It's time.


00:41:07.119 --> 00:41:09.980
The word, this lipstick drawing,


00:41:10.581 --> 00:41:15.580
I want it splashed over every newspaper,
every magazine, front page, national.


00:41:15.581 --> 00:41:16.804
The message ain't meant for us.


00:41:16.805 --> 00:41:19.405
Let's make sure it gets
to who it's intended for.


00:41:34.053 --> 00:41:35.240
Mr. Richard.


00:41:36.254 --> 00:41:38.508
- Marco.
- It's been a long time.


00:41:38.509 --> 00:41:40.273
Yes, it has.
How is the hand?


00:41:40.474 --> 00:41:43.192
It only hurts...
when it's humid.


00:41:43.193 --> 00:41:46.380
Well, you should've let us relocate you
to Arizona instead of New Orleans.


00:41:46.381 --> 00:41:49.535
Yeah, right,
but the boss likes it humid.


00:41:49.536 --> 00:41:50.875
He's waiting for you.


00:41:55.043 --> 00:41:56.197
What do you think?


00:41:56.969 --> 00:41:57.969
Hm?


00:41:57.970 --> 00:42:00.519
- Coincidence.
- Twenty-two times?


00:42:01.120 --> 00:42:03.264
A flower that only grows
in one place on earth?


00:42:04.058 --> 00:42:08.674
Couldn't it be the calling card of...
shoot, I forgot his name.


00:42:09.075 --> 00:42:10.595
What's his name,
your former partner,


00:42:10.596 --> 00:42:12.596
you know, the one who used to do
your wetwork?


00:42:14.564 --> 00:42:16.297
<i>- Fabio.
- Fabio.</i>


00:42:16.645 --> 00:42:18.499
Fabio Restrepo.


00:42:18.900 --> 00:42:19.818
May I?


00:42:22.581 --> 00:42:25.246
The CIA is not an amusement park.


00:42:25.647 --> 00:42:29.598
When the agency extracted your ass
from Colombia 15 years ago...


00:42:29.599 --> 00:42:33.183
and set you up here, we allowed you
to resume you little business,


00:42:33.184 --> 00:42:35.683
but what we should've done
was lock you away for life.


00:42:35.684 --> 00:42:39.358
Now, in exchange,
you should've kept the information flowing.


00:42:39.359 --> 00:42:41.509
- And I have.
- Not much.


00:42:43.920 --> 00:42:46.858
- I have nothing to do with this.
- Then find out who did.


00:43:01.717 --> 00:43:03.022
She's talking to us.


00:43:04.599 --> 00:43:05.858
Could be anyone.


00:43:06.864 --> 00:43:11.784
You idiot. I told you,
everyone dead, down to the dog.


00:43:14.091 --> 00:43:15.781
You screwed it up the first time.


00:43:16.582 --> 00:43:18.972
Now, go fix it.


00:45:13.120 --> 00:45:16.779
Each and every one of the victims
was a professional bad apple.


00:45:16.780 --> 00:45:19.488
As for motive,
I'm narrowing it down to, uh...


00:45:19.489 --> 00:45:21.889
payback, but, um...
not much else.


00:45:21.989 --> 00:45:24.545
My best guess, Alexa Milshinova,


00:45:24.946 --> 00:45:30.446
she made a career out of getting intimate
with high stake gamblers out of Vegas.


00:45:30.546 --> 00:45:34.133
She would, uh... rip 'em off and then
send them to meet their maker.


00:45:34.545 --> 00:45:36.801
Here.
D'Angelo James.


00:45:37.202 --> 00:45:39.998
He tried to take over the heroin trade
from Houston


00:45:41.586 --> 00:45:43.898
From the, uh...
Gemini Cartel.


00:45:44.099 --> 00:45:47.112
If you do not know, all there is to know
about these twins...


00:45:48.013 --> 00:45:49.713
you should not be in this room.


00:45:52.933 --> 00:45:53.833
Now you see,


00:45:53.834 --> 00:45:57.144
he tilts the camera just enough,
so he won't be seen going into the cell.


00:45:57.245 --> 00:45:59.628
The Time:
1:55 am.


00:45:59.629 --> 00:46:02.487
That means that our perp
was in that station, that...


00:46:03.488 --> 00:46:05.560
I don't have to spell it out for you,
do I?


00:46:06.400 --> 00:46:09.891
Excuse me.
Hand these out, please.


00:46:10.892 --> 00:46:14.410
These are the names, addresses
and phone numbers of everyone...


00:46:14.411 --> 00:46:19.078
with a pulse who was in that station
before 1:55 am.


00:46:19.679 --> 00:46:23.505
Everyone.
Which means one of them was our target.


00:46:23.706 --> 00:46:27.468
I want you to locate the ten people
in the folder you've just been handed.


00:46:27.469 --> 00:46:31.827
I want a detailed dossier on each of them
for the last ten years of their lives.


00:46:32.128 --> 00:46:36.010
I want you to run down every lead,
we will check every story.


00:46:36.011 --> 00:46:38.787
'Coz our killer, ladies and gentleman,
is in those folders...


00:46:38.888 --> 00:46:41.810
and I mean to catch him
before he kills again.


00:47:12.235 --> 00:47:13.402
Don't move.


00:47:17.643 --> 00:47:18.845
Hello, Jennifer.


00:47:20.358 --> 00:47:21.663
Hello, Danny.


00:47:33.675 --> 00:47:34.906
You haven't finished painting.


00:47:36.107 --> 00:47:38.909
Never really finished painting,
I just stopped working on it.


00:47:38.910 --> 00:47:40.525
I know something
you're gonna finish.


00:47:50.022 --> 00:47:51.173
Tell me something.


00:47:53.271 --> 00:47:55.086
Are we ever gonna go
on a normal date together?


00:47:55.087 --> 00:47:56.287
What's a normal date?


00:47:56.787 --> 00:48:00.113
Well, you know. Go out, have dinner,
drink wine, get drunk.


00:48:00.314 --> 00:48:01.771
Hm...
Dessert?


00:49:19.944 --> 00:49:24.836
- Safe?
- From my end. And you?


00:49:25.569 --> 00:49:28.176
- Safe.
- How's Mama?


00:49:29.563 --> 00:49:33.929
- She... is missing you.
- Well, tell her I miss her back.


00:49:34.130 --> 00:49:37.069
I think
she would love to hear that from you.


00:49:37.070 --> 00:49:38.070
I know.


00:49:39.070 --> 00:49:40.296
What do we got?


00:49:43.897 --> 00:49:47.651
Remember the guy on the news for running
a Ponzi scheme about a year ago?


00:49:47.652 --> 00:49:48.551
Mh-hm.


00:49:48.552 --> 00:49:52.172
Made 50 million dollars and vanished
into thin air. Clever guy.


00:49:52.173 --> 00:49:53.727
Now he's living in the Caribbean.


00:49:53.828 --> 00:49:55.128
- No.
- Mh...


00:49:55.228 --> 00:50:02.104
So, he left a lot of people very upset.
Want to give him a break, permanently.


00:50:08.360 --> 00:50:09.705
There's something else.


00:50:14.566 --> 00:50:16.750
How long has this been going on?


00:50:21.933 --> 00:50:25.731
- Not long.
- The newspaper says, 22.


00:50:26.632 --> 00:50:29.054
- Why?
- You know why.


00:50:29.455 --> 00:50:32.542
You think this is going to smoke
Don Luis out? You think he's that stupid?


00:50:32.743 --> 00:50:35.512
It's not just about you, okay?
Cataleya?


00:50:36.013 --> 00:50:38.346
There's me, Mama, and my family.


00:50:38.447 --> 00:50:40.290
- Familia?
- Okay.


00:50:40.491 --> 00:50:41.591
Tio, please.


00:50:42.891 --> 00:50:46.937
You're clean. You book the work,
you collect the money...


00:50:46.938 --> 00:50:50.014
The problem is,
I watch your back, that's why.


00:50:50.515 --> 00:50:54.572
Each and every job,
I make a dollar with, if I give you a job,


00:50:54.673 --> 00:50:58.958
I turn down five, ten, because
I made a promise to keep you safe.


00:50:59.494 --> 00:51:04.218
I'll keep you safe. Cataleya, that is
a full-time job, no matter what you think.


00:51:04.319 --> 00:51:07.107
But this is not a professional,
it's not what I do...


00:51:07.108 --> 00:51:10.730
I don't care, about what's professional
and what's safe. I'm doing this my way.


00:51:10.831 --> 00:51:12.836
- That is your way?
- Yeah.


00:51:13.137 --> 00:51:18.623
A dead killer, is stupid.


00:51:21.882 --> 00:51:23.582
Please, start listen...


00:51:25.183 --> 00:51:26.889
I should never have let you do this.


00:51:29.190 --> 00:51:35.218
You didn't let me do anything.
I chose this, remember? I chose this...


00:51:36.655 --> 00:51:38.879
From the first moment
I walked in your door,


00:51:39.180 --> 00:51:41.380
- I had already made my decision.
- By yourself?


00:51:41.381 --> 00:51:42.481
Yes.


00:51:44.451 --> 00:51:46.679
Not you, or anybody,
are gonna change that.


00:51:51.311 --> 00:51:53.454
We love you, Cataleya.


00:51:58.978 --> 00:52:01.228
Then watch my back
until it's done.


00:52:15.317 --> 00:52:16.417
Cataleya.


00:52:17.318 --> 00:52:19.543
- Excuse me?
- It's an orchid.


00:52:20.344 --> 00:52:22.786
- That's what this is?
- Sure does.


00:52:22.887 --> 00:52:25.133
- It grows in Colombia.
- How do you know that?


00:52:25.134 --> 00:52:26.845
My wife, she's Colombian.


00:52:28.924 --> 00:52:31.852
- Uh, uh... Cataleya?
- That's right.


00:52:43.160 --> 00:52:44.682
AMAZON


00:52:46.295 --> 00:52:48.470
Let's try 'organization'.


00:52:49.971 --> 00:52:51.671
What's this shit?


00:52:59.737 --> 00:53:02.019
Hi, boys.
Did you miss me?


00:53:03.362 --> 00:53:05.236
I've missed you too.


00:53:07.362 --> 00:53:09.008
Hi. Come!


00:53:10.984 --> 00:53:13.176
Have you guys been good?
Hm?


00:53:13.277 --> 00:53:14.774
Alright.
Stay.


00:53:15.975 --> 00:53:19.188
Sirloin...
Juicy.


00:53:19.189 --> 00:53:22.683
Delicious.
Want one?


00:53:22.884 --> 00:53:23.823
Good.


00:53:31.121 --> 00:53:32.073
Eat.


00:53:41.631 --> 00:53:45.615
I know that song.


00:53:46.268 --> 00:53:49.171
- I guess the boys gave me away, huh?
- You spoil them.


00:53:49.172 --> 00:53:50.322
I train them.

